2984 0 obj
<</A 2985 0 R/Alt("Three graphs show beta decay energy spectra for the isotopes superscript 3 BaseLine H, superscript 14 BaseLine C, and superscript 32 BaseLine P on Cartesian coordinate planes. The vertical axis of each graph is labeled Intensity, and the horizontal axis is labeled Energy \(M e V\). The first graph represents superscript 3 BaseLine H with E subscript max BaseLine equals 0.018 M e V. The horizontal axis ranges from 0 to 0.015 M e V in increments of 0.005 M e V. The curve begins near the vertical axis at moderate intensity, rises slightly to a peak near low energy values, then gradually decreases and approaches the horizontal axis near 0.018 M e V. The second graph represents superscript 14 BaseLine C with E subscript max BaseLine equals 0.156 M e V. The horizontal axis ranges from 0 to 0.15 M e V in increments of 0.05 M e V. The curve starts at moderate intensity, rises slightly to a rounded peak at low energy values, then steadily decreases toward the horizontal axis near 0.15 M e V. The third graph represents superscript 32 BaseLine P with E subscript max BaseLine equals 1.7 M e V. The horizontal axis ranges from 0 to 1.5 M e V in increments of 0.5 M e V. The curve begins above the horizontal axis at near the vertical axis, rises to a broad maximum near the middle of the graph around 0.5 to 0.7 M e V, then decreases steadily and approaches the horizontal axis near 1.5 to 1.7 M e V.\r\nNote: All the values are approximate."\r\n␀)/ID(e8382bdd77a5b8679d480cbf)/K 123/P 2562 0 R/Pg 2269 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
2985 0 obj
<</BBox[70.8 226.8 564 387.6]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>
endobj
2986 0 obj
<</ID(d88bd6d4902b7ae7a4ac53e4)/K[124 125 126 127 128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136 137]/P 2562 0 R/Pg 2269 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
2987 0 obj
<</A 2988 0 R/Alt("A graph titled Penetration Ability of Beta RadiationŽ shows the penetration range of beta particles for different materials on a Cartesian coordinate plane. The horizontal axis is labeled Energy \(M e V\) and ranges from 0.1 to 4 M e V on a logarithmic scale. The vertical axis is labeled Maximum Range of Beta Particles \(Inches\) and ranges from 0.001 to 1000 inches on a logarithmic scale. Several upward-sloping lines represent the penetration range of beta particles in different materials, including air, water, plastic \(Lucite\), concrete, aluminum, glass, iron, lead, and copper.  The line labeled Air appears highest on the graph, beginning near \(0.1, 7\) and increasing steadily to \(4, 700\). The line labeled Water begins near \(0.1, 0.008\) and rises to \(4, 0.9\). The line labeled Plastic \(Lucite\) begins near \(0.1, 0.007\) and increases to \(4, 0.7\). The line labeled Concrete begins near \(0.1, 0.005\) and rises to \(4, 0.6\). The line labeled Aluminum begins near \(0.1, 0.003\) and increases to approximately \(4, 0.4\). The line labeled Glass begins near \(0.1, 0.004\) and rises to \(4, 0.5\). The line labeled Iron begins near \(0.13, 0.001\) and increases to \(4, 0.11\). The line labeled Lead begins near \(0.14, 0.001\) and rises to \(4, 0.09\). The line labeled Copper begins near \(0.15, 0.001\) and increases to \(4, 0.08\).\r\nNote: All the values are approximate."\r\n␀)/ID(bdf32bc4b85bd55d8805a5f4)/K 0/P 2562 0 R/Pg 2273 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
2988 0 obj
<</BBox[70.8 153.6 525 722.4]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>
