2999 0 obj
<</A 3000 0 R/Alt("A scatter plot shows the relative intensity of photon energy on a Cartesian coordinate plane. The vertical axis is labeled Relative Intensity. The horizontal axis is labeled Photon energy \(k e V\) and ranges from 0 to 800 k e V in increments of 50 k e V. The plotted data begins near 0 k e V at high intensity, drops slightly near 20 k e V to moderate-high intensity, and remains approximately flat with small fluctuations from about 20 to 450 k e V. A small raised bump appears near 180 k e V at slightly higher intensity, after which the plot returns to the nearly flat baseline.\r\nBeginning near 450 k e V at moderate intensity, the data decreases steadily and reaches a minimum near 580 k e V at low intensity. The plot then rises sharply from about 600 k e V to a prominent peak near 660 k e V at maximum intensity. After the peak, the data drops steeply near 720 k e V to low intensity. Beyond 720 k e V, sparse scattered points continue at very low intensity values and gradually approach near-zero intensity by approximately 900 k e V.\r\nNote: All values are approximate."\r\n␀)/ID(cdf3a1687b0be5a66acb904f)/K 47/P 2562 0 R/Pg 2277 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
