3241 0 obj
<</A 3242 0 R/Alt("A diagram and graph show the production and energy spectrum of X-rays. On the left side, the diagram illustrates an angled target structure and is labeled AnodeŽ below it. The upper horizontal portion of the anode is labeled 120 k V.Ž An electron labeled e superscript minus is shown traveling along a curved path toward the angled surface of the anode. A wavy line extending downward from the point of impact represents emitted X-ray radiation. Three electrons labeled ""e superscript minus"" are shown as horizontal dashed lines moving from left to right toward a coiled spiral structure labeled ""Cathode"" at the bottom. The cathode is connected to a line labeled ""0 V"" at the top. On the right side, a graph shows Relative Intensity versus Photon Energy \(k e V\) on a Cartesian coordinate plane. The horizontal axis is labeled Photon Energy \(k e V\) and ranges from 0 to 120 k e V in increments of 10 k e V. The vertical axis is labeled Relative Intensity. The curve begins near 5 k e V at zero intensity, rises steeply to moderate intensity by about 20 k e V, and continues increasing to a broad maximum near 45 to 50 k e V. After the peak, the curve gradually decreases as photon energy increases, approaching zero intensity near 120 k e V. Several narrow vertical peaks appear above the smooth curve near 58, 67, and 72 k e V.\r\nNote: All values are approximate."\r\n␀)/ID(7a70b422aea96e35a29e9793)/K[56 57 58 59 60 61 62 63 64 65 66 67 68 69 70 71 72 73 74 75 76 77]/P 2562 0 R/Pg 2188 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>
