<</A 3322 0 R/Alt(A diagram illustrates the working principle of an ionization chamber. A small circle on the left represents a radiation source emitting several wavy arrows directed toward the right. One of the wavy arrows strikes an interaction point marked with a star in the central region between two parallel plates. From the interaction point, a positively charged particle labeled ionŽ marked with a plus symbol moves upward toward the upper plate, and an electron labeled e superscript minus moves downward toward the lower plate. Several small dots are scattered in the region between the plates. The upper plate is shown with negative charge symbols, and the lower plate is shown with positive charge symbols. The upper plate is connected to one end of an ammeter. The other end of the ammeter is connected to the negative terminal of a battery. The lower plate is connected to the positive terminal of the battery.\r\n␀)/ID(1aae4c6da1ae2a24bae4980a)/K 0/P 2562 0 R/Pg 2161 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>
