<</A 3327 0 R/Alt(A graph shows signal versus applied voltage on a Cartesian coordinate plane. The vertical axis is labeled Signal, and the horizontal axis is labeled Applied Voltage. The graph is divided into five regions labeled 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 by four vertical boundary lines. The plotted curve begins near the origin at very low signal values in Region 1 and rises steeply before leveling slightly near the boundary between Regions 1 and 2. In Region 2, the curve increases gradually with a small positive slope. In Region 3, the curve rises more rapidly with a steeper slope through the middle portion of the graph. In Region 4, the curve continues increasing at a slower rate and begins to level off. In Region 5, the curve rises sharply again toward the upper right corner of the graph.\r\n␀)/ID(df0470b46339bc32b444fb2e)/K 25/P 2562 0 R/Pg 2161 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>
