<</A 3419 0 R/Alt(A pie chart titled "All Categories S and E subscript U S" shows the percentage contribution of various sources of radiation exposure. The chart is divided into multiple sectors, each labeled with a source category and percentage contribution. The largest sector on the right side represents Radon and thoron \(background\) at 37 percent. A large sector on the left represents Computed tomography \(medical\) at 24 percent. Another large sector near the lower left represents Nuclear medicine \(medical\) at 12 percent. A sector near the bottom represents Interventional fluoroscopy \(medical\) at 7 percent. Another sector near the lower right represents Conventional radiography or fluoroscopy \(medical\) at 5 percent. Near the top of the chart, one sector represents Space \(background\) at 5 percent, and another sector represents Internal \(background\) at 5 percent. A smaller sector represents Terrestrial \(background\) at 3 percent. Another small sector represents Consumer at 2 percent. Two very small sectors on the right side represent Occupational and Industrial, each labeled less than 0.1 percent.\r\n␀)/ID(929537ea1b7e537b73d597ec)/K 0/P 2562 0 R/Pg 2052 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>
